#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0422 expect=noViolation domain=SJ
#library standard=sendig-dart version=1-2
#note "Both neighbours carry the SAME month-precision value 2020-01. Under IsoDateComparison's forall-hull rule '2020-01 <= 2020-01' is FALSE (upper 2020-01-31 > lower 2020-01-01), so a relation that replaced the identity comparison would newly FIRE on a pair the equality-only rule accepted - a narrowing nobody ruled. D-1's disjunction keeps it silent. This scenario is the regression detector for that, and it must not be 'simplified' to complete dates."
dataset SJ label="Subject Stages"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col SJSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col SJSTDTC type=Char label="Start Date/Time of Repro Stage"
col SJENDTC type=Char label="End Date/Time of Repro Stage"
---
STUDY01 | SJ | R-003 | 1 | 2019-12 | 2020-01
STUDY01 | SJ | R-003 | 2 | 2020-01 | 2020-03-15
---
